{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You saw what I did to Egypt.</b> How much I pressed them, so that they would turn back from their wickedness — for I do not desire the death of the dying. But when they hardened their necks, I was compelled to multiply My signs and wonders among them and to destroy them." "<b>And I bore you on eagles' wings.</b> By a path through which no person had passed — like the eagle that leads its young through the height of the air, where no other species of bird goes — and this was to separate you from all the peoples and their pursuits, to be Mine." "<b>And I brought you to Me.</b> To the mountain of Elohim, prepared for prophecy."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:15.454717570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}